    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Dooley Poynton Auctioneers are delighted to present this truly unique opportunity to acquire a historical 19th Century period Townhouse Property occupying a prominent position on the main street of Hacketstown, Co. Carlow. This property is steeped in local history formally serving as a 19th Century Courthouse with many stories to tell. This unique property recently operated as the village credit union and is currently seeking planning permission for change of use from a commercial office into a residential home. This historic property presents a blank canvas, offering a discerning buyer the opportunity to reconfigure and redesign the interior into a contemporary styled two-storey residence. The property boasts a well portioned private rear garden providing a tranquil outdoor setting nestled away from the bustling village life. Hacketstown is located at the foothills of the Wicklow Mountains with many walking trails and is within a 30-minute drive from the coast. Intriguing, Genealogists have traced the ancestral roots of Elvis Presley's great-great-great-great-grandfather, William Presley, back to the village of Hacketstown. One “can’t help falling in love” with this property boasting a vibrant village lifestyle with a selection of shops, Supervalu, Londis, Kennedy’s Pharmacy & Medical Hall & the highly rated “Brew Stop Café”, right on your doorstep, along with St. Josephs National School & Coláiste Eoin Secondary School. Viewing is by appointment only. \r\nA.M.V €195,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Description \r\n\r\nStorm Porch/Entrance Hallway (c.1.79m x 2.75m) \r\nThis entrance hallway leads into the main reception area. \r\nThis area features ceramic tiled floor and ceiling lighting.\r\n\r\n\r\nBanking Hall/Main Reception Room (c.2.00m x 3.63m) + (c.3.24m x 2.78m)\r\nThe Reception is situated overlooking the front of the property. This space boasts three counter spaces with sliding windows and a spacious waiting area. This space features fluorescent lighting and ceramic tiled flooring throughout. This space features a door leading to the attic room.   \r\n\r\n\r\nBack Office/Meeting Room (c.4.91mx 4.17m)\r\nThis meeting room features dual aspect overlooking the street view and the rear garden area. This space features a small built-in kitchenette with a stainless-steel sink, strobe lighting & ceramic tiled flooring throughout. A door leads to the rear hallway. \r\n\r\n\r\nRear Hallway + Safe Room +Guest W/C (c.2.39m x 3.14m)\r\nThe rear hallway leads to the Safe Room, Guest W/C and provides access to the rear garden area. The guest W/C features a toilet, a ceramic wash hand basin and ceramic tiled flooring throughout. \r\n\r\n\r\nAttic Storage Area (c.4.91m x 7.55m) + Stairwell (c.4.91m x 0.93m)\r\nThis spacious attic space features angled ceilings and strobe lighting.\r\n\r\n\r\nGarden Area \r\nThe property features a generously proportioned garden. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nServices: \r\n•\tMains Water\r\n•\tMains Sewerage \r\n•\tOFCH \r\n•\tBER: D BER NO:T.B.C \r\n•\tEnergy Performance Indicator:T.B.C"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tPeriod Townhouse c.55m2 situated on the main street, Hacketstown, Co.Carlow.\r\n•\tThe property offers a well-proportioned rear garden.\r\n•\tThis property offers a blank canvas to create your dream home. \r\n•\tThere is wheelchair access into the property.\r\n•\tVillage centre location with all local amenities on your doorstep.\r\n•\tChange of Use Planning Ref: 26/60284"
      },
